# Coverage exclusions (dte coverage). An artifact that cites no decision BECAUSE no decision
# governs it goes here, under the reason it needs none, so 100% coverage is reachable and
# means something. A "why:" line opens a group; the globs under it (.dteignore syntax) belong
# to it. Excluded files are still scanned: a citation inside one still counts, and a glob
# that matches nothing is reported as stale. Everything not listed here is expected to cite.

why: package manifests, toolchain and CI configuration serve the build, not a product decision
package.json
package-lock.json
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.node.json
vercel.json
index.html
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.mcp.json
.dteignore
.vscode
.github
.impeccable
src/vite-env.d.ts
tests/setup
src-tauri/Cargo.toml
src-tauri/build.rs
src-tauri/tauri.conf.json
src-tauri/tauri.live.conf.json
src-tauri/.gitignore
src-tauri/.cargo
src-tauri/capabilities
packages/*/package.json
obsidian-plugin/manifest.json
public/robots.txt
public/sitemap.xml

why: licences and the product pitch are reader on-ramps, not system descriptions (author's rule 2026-09-18)
LICENSE
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
README.md
PRODUCT.md

